  "configuration_id": "config_017",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_016 (multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, concat) achieved 0.527 acc / 0.510 F1, a meaningful +4.2% improvement over rna-only baseline (config_001), confirming that image features add value. However, we have only tested one fusion strategy (concat). Uncertainty: We do not know whether weighted fusion could further improve or degrade performance relative to simple concatenation. This experiment (config_017) isolates exactly one variable—changing fusion from concat to weighted—while holding model_setting, profile_setting, RNA encoder, and image encoder identical to config_016. This gives a clean causal read on fusion strategy. Why best next: Under a tight budget, a single-variable comparison against our current best result is the most information-dense experiment. The outcome directly determines whether all future multimodal configurations should default to weighted or concat fusion, effectively halving the remaining search space. It is a low-risk exploitation step that also reduces a key design uncertainty before we invest experiments in larger architectural changes (multiprofile, ViT-L, alternative RNA encoders)."
}

